---
import SocialIcons from "../components/SocialIcons.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  name: SITE.name,
  url: SITE.url,
  email: SITE.email,
  jobTitle: SITE.role,
  worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: SITE.employer },
  sameAs: [SITE.youtube, SITE.github, SITE.linkedin],
};
---

<PageLayout
  title="About"
  description="Backend engineer at Jio Platforms. Public CS curriculum on YouTube. Mumbai."
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />

  <section class="wrap py-16 sm:py-20">
    <p class="section-kicker">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
      {SITE.name}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-accent">{SITE.tagline}</p>
    <div class="rule-cyan mt-5"></div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_18rem]">
      <div class="max-w-[46rem] space-y-6 text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p class="text-ink">
          Backend engineer at Jio Platforms (Jio Cloud / India AI), Mumbai. Java, Spring Boot, distributed systems. 2.5+ years.
        </p>
        <p>
          I design infrastructure that has to be wrong in public: quota checks that fail before provision, queues that do not block the caller, replication that has a known recovery path. The rest of this site is how I wish that kind of work had been taught.
        </p>
        <p>
          Currently filming Season 1 of a public CS curriculum — whiteboard, then interview problems, then a small project you can run. Notes live here. YouTube is the class.
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink">Jio Platforms</h2>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-faint">Software Development Engineer I · Dec 2023 – present</p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-accent">
          <li>
            Quota validation framework for Jio Cloud across ROS, HCI, GCP, and internal IaaS. Logical and physical checks before provision, so over-commit fails at the source instead of after.
          </li>
          <li>
            Central engine on order types — VMs, block storage, security groups, HSM — which cut post-provisioning failure orders by about 40% in the numbers we tracked.
          </li>
          <li>
            Async order-processing pipeline on RabbitMQ for compute, storage, and networking across hybrid cloud.
          </li>
          <li>
            OPS logging with end-to-end traces on provisioning failures. Incident close time dropped about 60% on the paths we instrumented.
          </li>
          <li>
            Disaster recovery: REST API work and asynchronous replication workflows with infrastructure teams. Not a one-person feature; I was a core contributor.
          </li>
          <li>
            Scheduled PostgreSQL–Oracle sync so order state (Postgres) and provisioning state (Oracle) do not drift.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-faint">
          Java 17 · Spring Boot · Spring MVC · PostgreSQL · Oracle · RabbitMQ · Redis · Hibernate/JPA · REST · Maven · Linux
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink">Stack</h2>
        <p>
          Java is the primary language. Spring Boot, Spring MVC, Spring Data JPA, Hibernate. PostgreSQL, Oracle, Redis, RabbitMQ. Docker, Kubernetes, Maven, Git. Distributed systems, async processing, event-driven design. Spring AI and the Claude API on the side project, not on the day job.
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink">Education</h2>
        <p>
          B.E. Computer Science, Honours in Data Science — PVGCOE, Nashik (Pune Vidhyarthi Griha’s College of Engineering), Jun 2019 – Aug 2023. CGPA 8.60.
        </p>
        <p>
          Completed the Certified Kubernetes Application Developer (CKAD) course on Coursera. That is the course, not the Linux Foundation exam.
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink">Elsewhere</h2>
        <p>
          Earlier: Kavach, an Android SOS app (Java, XML, Firebase). Gold medal at Anveshana 2023; shortlisted for the Government of India Tech Innovation Awards. It is not a curriculum build and it is not listed under Projects.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="h-fit border border-line bg-canvas-elevated p-5">
        <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-widest text-faint uppercase">Now</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">Filming Season 1 · Memory &amp; Low-Level</p>
        <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-widest text-faint uppercase">Mail</p>
        <a class="mt-2 block text-sm text-accent hover:underline break-all" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
        <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-widest text-faint uppercase">Socials</p>
        <div class="mt-3">
          <SocialIcons />
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
